{"resourceIdentifier":"1760","resourceName":"The Haidar EL ALI Mangrove Initiative (HEAMI)","description":"The proposed project activities is a plan for the reforestation of the degraded lands in the mangrove patches of Senegal. The stated goal of the project activity is to restore degraded wetlands. In doing so, the program will contribute to the mitigation of climate change through the removal of greenhouse gases. On the other hand, the project activity contributes to sustainable development through providing permanent and temporary employment and numerous economic and social benefits to thousands of households in the villages within the project’s vicinity. The project will strengthen the regional economies alleviating poverty for local communities of the host country. Awareness, training and technical assistance in mangrove establishment, environmental conservation and sustainable ecosystem management will also be provided to local people.This project was open for public comment from 4 May - 3 June 2018. Comments received are included in the PUB_COM_1760_11JUN2018 document.","location":{"latitude":14.570555,"longitude":-16.574165},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1760"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Casamance, Sine Saloum"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Withdrawn"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"30170"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-AMS0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"t